WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.030
My robot was supposed to reach the target.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.540
It walked into the wall instead!

3
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.710
Something in my program was wrong.

4
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.410
Today: bugs, and how to find and fix them.

5
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.140
A mistake in a program is called a bug.

6
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.520
Every programmer makes bugs,

7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:20.900
even the best ones.

8
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.510
Finding and fixing them is

9
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:24.110
called debugging.

10
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.620
It’s like being a detective.

11
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.660
First, run the program

12
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.840
and watch carefully.

13
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:32.820
Where does the robot go?

14
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.250
Point to the first card where

15
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.330
it goes the wrong way.

16
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.340
Then change just that one card.

17
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.400
Don’t change everything!

18
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.140
Run it again and see if it works.

19
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.280
If not, find the next wrong card.

20
00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.010
A detective doesn’t guess.

21
00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.530
She looks for clues, one at a time.

22
00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.930
You do the same: watch, find the

23
00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.290
clue, fix, and check again.

24
00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.120
Quick check!

25
00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.950
The robot should go forward,

26
00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.890
turn right, forward.

27
00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.660
My cards say forward, turn left, forward.

28
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.970
Which card is the bug?

29
00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:16.780
The turn!

30
00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:18.630
It should be turn right.

31
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.780
Change only that card, run it again,

32
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.840
and the robot reaches the target.

33
00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.180
Programmers often write the cards

34
00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.620
as words, one on each line.

35
00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.140
This is the same program, written as code.

36
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.400
Each line is one card.

37
00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.010
Can you read it?

38
00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:41.070
In the app, open Program a robot

39
00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.730
and try grids five and six.

40
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.820
When the robot bumps, find the first

41
00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.680
wrong card and fix only that one.

42
00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:51.620
Your turn.

43
00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.240
Your robot bumps into a wall.

44
00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.120
What do you do first?

45
00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.280
Find the first wrong card.

46
00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.420
Remember: a bug is a mistake,

47
00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.420
and everyone makes them.

48
00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.690
Test, find the first wrong step,

49
00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.570
change one thing, and test again.

50
00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.720
Try it yourself: hide a bug.

51
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.480
Draw a robot path on paper, write the

52
00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:20.300
cards, and put one wrong card in.

53
00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.640
Can a friend or someone at

54
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.780
home find your bug?
